          {
            title: 'Three Card Poker',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Three Card Poker is a popular casino table game based on poker. Players compete against the dealer. It features two modes of play: Ante/Play (playing against the dealer) and Pair Plus (betting on the hand value alone). It is known for its speed and simplicity.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Three Card Poker was invented in England in the mid 1990s by Derek Webb. It was originally called Casino Brag, inspired by 3-card Brag, and was adapted so players bet against the house rather than each other. The name Three Card Poker was adopted when the game was introduced to America; it is also known as Tri Poker. Derek Webb's Prime Table Games marketed it to casinos; in 1999 Shuffle Master (later SHFL Entertainment) acquired the rights.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Dealer + 1-6 Players',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Casino table, chips',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3 cards to each player and dealer.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
